{"title":"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(x_as_smallest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (x as smallest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(x_as_middle_number)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (x as middle number)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of five consecutive odd integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. The smallest of these integers is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddc609a3bc616a7555017c3ff8b2b34f61e4b68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 17 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 19 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 21 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 25 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28x_as_smallest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(x_as_smallest)\">Solution 1 (x as smallest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (x as smallest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest of the five integers. Since the numbers are consecutive odd integers, the full list of numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4ff6c2a55f8234cc3d9fd74bde83d083dcb8c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, x + 2, x + 4, x + 6, x + 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />. The sum of these numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6944d3715f1b4d16771849d63b23c96dd56b6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + x + 2 + x + 4 + x + 6 + x + 8 = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"319\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b35b2abdbfa3889fd50a820aca0d9b6446a5d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x + 20 = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f77a4050fb33d5353d8ff28834ee1a119561c325.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x = 125 - 20 = 105$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"165\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/518ea5e77626bdf2ad03db02abe90a803ce47642.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{105}{5} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28x_as_middle_number.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(x_as_middle_number)\">Solution 2 (x as middle number)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (x as middle number)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the middle number of the five integers. Since the numbers are consecutive odd integers, the full list of numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/4190761c4f91a053b95c46ecf0be97d5341f8345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 4, x - 2, x, x + 2, x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />. The sum of these numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/3856e666063486e6430aae3ea2519eafb475244c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 4 + x - 2 + x + x + 2 + x + 4 = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"319\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e4a3f5973bd8914c6e6305a707275f181b644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc06a158c32dd9cf784456ce249f68a7fad1a819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{125}{5} = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The smallest number is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b43538a4b1b97656c4abce33ab14d268d2f9c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 4 = 25 - 4 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"206\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>This solution can be useful because all of the constant terms cancel out.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 3 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can try different sums for the numbers using different answer choices, starting with the middle answer choice. \n</p><p>If the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then the full list of numbers would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a0fe66e0660ff04ade5cfb098cf9d4499084b9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21, 23, 25, 27, 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"17\" />. The sum would then be:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/1853af24e3c90aca50fa687a8c8abe4afab94efe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 + 23 + 25 + 27 + 29 = 69 + 56 = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"316\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>This exactly matches the actual sum of the numbers, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02c3f25464453a3f118d7275f4ffcc4e2dd08390.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley\">2024 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&